<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-OPINION-Louthean on Australian Mining: Plutonic growing.</title>
<headline>RTRS-OPINION-Louthean on Australian Mining: Plutonic growing.</headline>
<dateline>PERTH 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>*By Ross Louthean</p>
<p>Plutonic Resources Ltd is the company which produced a mine that keeps on growing at a spectacular rate and gave project payback in its first nine months of operation.</p>
<p>Named after its Plutonic mine in the Glengarry Basin, north of Meekatharra in Western Australia, the company has used its accumulating mining profits as a war chest to take control of base metals prospector Lachlan Resources NL buy the Forsayth group of gold mining companies and, more recently, picked up Archaean Gold NL</p>
</text>
